{"title":"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number you receive.\n</p><p>A box contains pears, apples, and oranges. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> pears, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apples, and the number of oranges is one-third the number of apples. A fruit is randomly chosen from the box. What is the probability that the fruit is an apple?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the number of oranges is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the number of apples and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apples, the number of oranges is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46bb2b0ea935df4882cab786b730e29cec50248f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{3} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>There would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> pears, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apples, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> oranges, so the total number of fruit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb19bc4c0c23649dd7f4350ca0e7f25ab055b72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N + 9 + 3 = N + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/0019e990a1438f9ff5acf64fcf6011216f844322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> fruit in total and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apples, meaning that the probability of picking an apple is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/494692cee5b4466e1b33fcc6e8ca4161563229d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{N + 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"63\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 3\">player 3</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a2b1091166a6e32e6ddaec65386d3e713011cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />. This means that the probability would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c635cdea6f1d004a99261b3ca7bd7ad98b843d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{12 + 12} = \\frac{9}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"111\" height=\"40\" />, which reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9fa5161e13b43f98f18554dc7c8af36d638c5e97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{3}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"26\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC\">2025 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 3\">Relay B Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 1\">Relay C Problem 1</a></b>\n</td></tr>\